 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5961+) **C++ inline-return cleanup:** collapsed simple inline DLL header functions whose bodies were exactly one `return` statement to one physical line, making trivial getters/wrappers easier to grep and compare. Done with the help of [`collapse_cpp_inline_returns.py`](/LLM_Helpers/README.md#collapse_cpp_inline_returnspy), a conservative mechanical helper that skips constructors/destructors, multi-statement bodies, body comments, multiline signatures, and overlong results. For example, `int getGoldPerTurnByPlayer(PlayerTypes ePlayer) const { return m_aiGoldPerTurnByPlayer.get(ePlayer); } // Exposed to Python`, instead of its old four-line equivalent.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5930+) **GitHub workflow build checks:** added GitHub Actions checks under [`.github/workflows`](/.github/workflows/) to catch forgotten debug/default settings and data drift at each commit. Current checks notably verify launch-guard sentinel values, XML tag references in SAS define text values, integer SAS define bounds, valid main-menu opening-music script setup, disabled BBAI logging defaults, shared UI font defaults, Sevopedia Leader AI Personality Panel predumped-cache defaults and predump file presence, `SAS_MAGIC_WORLDSIZE_*` constants matching `CIV4WorldInfo.xml` order, `CvGameCoreDLL/Project/temp_files/` staying effectively empty (only its tracked placeholder file), not being ignored by `.gitignore`, and being allowed only as an archive-excluded development marker through `.gitattributes` (helps catch stale fast-compile temp files. We check this because we suspect fast compiles can be unreliable, and also helps catch forgetting to replace the committed DLL after compiling; see [KI#38](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#38---no-idea-why-but-sometimes-compile-mysteriouslystrangelyinconsistently-fails-and-recompiling-succeeds-underwith-but-exact-same-source-files-if-i-am-not-mistaken-but) and [KI#38.2](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#382---weird-dll-xml-errors-at-launch-solved-by-recompiling-the-exact-same-dll-cosmic-ray-2-or-something-else-maybe-or-whatever-maybe-but)), and every playable `PrivateMaps/*.py` being listed exactly once across the SAS map-script heaviness/coverage defines while every listed map script exists in `PrivateMaps/`. For example, this helped spot [map scripts that were previously unclassified in SAS map-script heaviness defines](https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/actions/runs/27198308080/job/80295526028); they are now listed explicitly for exhaustiveness (more robust; no gameplay change).
 - Other examples: (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5935+) This notably also **helped spot and fix duplicate text, parent, and child XML keys** found by new GitHub workflow check [text](https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/actions/runs/27332010214/job/80746523894), [parent](https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/actions/runs/27258698041/job/80498936912), and [child](https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/actions/runs/27336768909/job/80762873956) (See [KI#148](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#148---fixed-base-advciv-issue-and-one-advciv-sas-issue-of-duplicate-parent-xml-keys-found-by-new-github-workflow-check), [KI#149](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#149---fixed-base-advciv-issue-duplicate-xml-text-tags-found-by-new-github-workflow-check), [KI#150](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#150---fixed-base-advciv-issue-and-some-advciv-sas-priority-duplicate-xml-childlist-entries-found-by-new-github-workflow-check)), and [suspicious malformed-looking XML tag punctuation](https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/actions/runs/27342682844/job/80783239087) (e.g., `<French>>`, `</English>>`) (see [KI#151](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#151---fixed-base-advciv-issue-suspicious-malformed-looking-xml-angle-tags-found-by-new-github-workflow-check)) and [XML suspicious text chars](https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/actions/runs/27400470104/job/80977135402) (see [KI#152](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#152---fixed-suspicious-replacement-question-marks-in-lengthy-sevopedia-xml-found-by-new-github-workflow-check)). The checks also run locally with Python 3; see [`.github/workflows/README.md` current build checks](/.github/workflows/README.md#current-build-checks).
+- (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5964+) **Python Ruff GitHub workflow:** added [`python-ruff.yml`](/.github/workflows/python-ruff.yml), which prints a full Ruff report and fails on a practical critical gate for syntax/parse errors and Pyflakes bug checks. This helped spot shadowed duplicate callbacks in base Civ4 `Oasis.py` (see [KI#164](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#164---fixed-base-civ4-oasis-map-script-had-shadowed-python-callbacks-found-by-the-python-ruff-github-workflow)) and a Base AdvCiv bug of dormant undefined `Point` (instead of using `PointLayout`) helper in `RectLayout.py` (see [KI#165](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues.md#165---fixed-dormant-rectlayout-upperleft-helper-returned-undefined-point-found-by-python-ruff)).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5962+) **Light source archive helper:** added [`make_light_source_zip.py`](/LLM_Helpers/README.md#make_light_source_zippy), which creates a timestamped no-compression AdvCiv-SAS source/data/docs archive under `LLM_Helpers/outputs` or a chosen output folder. This avoids repeatedly manually selecting and tediously creating an updated ZIP of each file/folder each time, of the same useful core files/folders ChatGPT or other LLMs can read or needs, while leaving unneeded or too heavy to use ones (e.g., as of now no .fpk, .tga, .dll, or pycache folders, art assets folder), when sharing compact mod context with local tools or LLMs.
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5931+) **Dependabot for GitHub Actions:** added Dependabot tracking for GitHub Actions versions to help address Node.js runtime deprecation warnings such as `actions/<hidden-email>` and `actions/<hidden-email>` still using Node.js 20 (see [<hidden-email>#24](https://github.com/wonderingabout/AdvCiv-SAS/pull/24)). This should reduce manual maintenance and make future action-version updates easier to notice and apply. See [`.github/workflows/README.md` current build checks](/.github/workflows/README.md#current-build-checks).
 - **Handicap XML comparison helper:** added [`compare_handicap_infos.py`](/LLM_Helpers/compare_handicap_infos.py), a report-only, mod-agnostic helper that compares two explicit `CIV4HandicapInfo.xml` file paths, inside or outside this mod folder, by handicap index; shows missing fields as blanks, includes absolute/percentage numeric deltas, and embeds a spreadsheet-friendly TSV matrix. The shipped stable example [`handicap_infos_compared.md`](/LLM_Helpers/examples/handicap_infos_compared.md) compares base AdvCiv 1.12 vs AdvCiv-SAS. See [LLM_Helpers (README.md)](/LLM_Helpers/README.md).

